codex
The symbolic domain is an arbitrary finite `IntSeq` whose elements satisfy a recursive non-negativity predicate; it is converted bijectively to the semantics’ Python-list representation. That avoids any fixed-size unrolling and covers all finite non-negative integer lists, including empty lists. The loop invariant will thread a `noPick | pick(value,index)` accumulator over the symbolic suffix.
